  "body": "LOT-162\nCloses #252\nClaim: cloud/lot-162-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5\n\n## Problem\nLists, navigation, accounts and settings had gaps for VoiceOver and low-vision users: the unread-pages and MP \"non lu\" capsules were white on light grey/cyan (1.5–1.7:1, #646), red and orange message text measured 2.2–3.6:1, banner and fold buttons were under 44 pt, spinners had no label, and async results (login error, search outcome, confirmations) were silent.\n\n## Change\nSpec `docs/lots/LOT-162-a11y-lists.md` (checklist, what was already fine). `AccessibleColors` (computed contrast, tested), `BadgeCapsule`, `StatusLabel`; 44 pt targets; spinner labels; \"N sujets\" header count; `.isSelected` on the current account; sliders no longer read twice; search result row combined; `AccessibilityNotification.Announcement` for banners, login error, search outcome; filtered-posts banner lifts its line limit at AX sizes. No behaviour change.\n\n## Tests\n`AccessibleColorsTests` (WCAG reference ratios, every badge/message colour ≥ 4.5:1 on white, black and the grouped greys, the old accent capsule < 2:1), `TopicRowCuesTests.topicCountLabel`. Not built in the cloud: reviewed with compiler rigour; CI is the first build.\n\n## Ledger\nNo entries.\n\n## Mac checks\n- Accessibility Inspector audit on each screen (iPhone 18 Pro, iPad, iOS 27.0)\n- VoiceOver pass: Favoris, Catégories, MP, accounts, login, settings, search\n- AX5 Dynamic Type, Increase Contrast, light and dark; capsule contrast on screenshots (#646)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHziq4RiUH8XHrkC9W)_",
